1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,330
NebiusGuard is a small Node.js client library for inspecting model streams

2
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:08,660
and tool arguments. This recording combines a captured real Nebius and

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:12,989
NVIDIA run with clearly labeled synthetic security cases. It is a

4
00:00:12,989 --> 00:00:15,351
prototype, not a deployed customer service.

5
00:00:15,851 --> 00:00:20,471
The client uses Nebius Token Factory for model discovery and chat

6
00:00:20,471 --> 00:00:25,091
completions. Applications call a separate tool-validation boundary. Streamed responses pass through

7
00:00:25,091 --> 00:00:29,711
credential-pattern checks before callbacks receive them. The audit log links events

8
00:00:29,711 --> 00:00:32,651
with hashes; it is not immutable storage.

9
00:00:33,151 --> 00:00:37,316
This is evidence from an actual authenticated run, not a mock

10
00:00:37,316 --> 00:00:41,481
response. The client discovered thirty account-visible models and selected NVIDIA Nemotron

11
00:00:41,481 --> 00:00:45,646
three Nano, thirty B, A three B. It then streamed an

12
00:00:45,646 --> 00:00:49,811
answer through the real Token Factory endpoint. No API key appears

13
00:00:49,811 --> 00:00:50,947
in this recording.

14
00:00:51,447 --> 00:00:55,741
The returned answer explains why cloud-metadata requests can expose instance credentials

15
00:00:55,741 --> 00:01:00,034
and create a network pivot. The run reports the Nebius Token

16
00:01:00,034 --> 00:01:04,328
Factory provider path, two audit events, and a valid local hash

17
00:01:04,328 --> 00:01:08,621
chain. This proves one integration smoke test, not model accuracy or

18
00:01:08,621 --> 00:01:09,402
production performance.

19
00:01:09,902 --> 00:01:15,096
These next cases are synthetic and never contact their targets. URL

20
00:01:15,096 --> 00:01:20,289
normalization prevents alternate representations from bypassing the static checks. Metadata, integer-form

21
00:01:20,289 --> 00:01:25,483
loopback, private ten-dot addresses, and uppercase localhost are all rejected. DNS

22
00:01:25,483 --> 00:01:29,260
resolution and redirects still belong to the executor.

23
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:34,457
A streaming detector cannot recall bytes already delivered. The sanitizer therefore

24
00:01:34,457 --> 00:01:39,153
retains a thirty-nine-character suffix, derived from the supported patterns. This synthetic

25
00:01:39,153 --> 00:01:43,850
split-credential case rejects before any credential characters reach the callback. Benign

26
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:47,692
withheld text is released only after a complete stream.

27
00:01:48,192 --> 00:01:52,388
If an SSE response ends without its terminal marker, the client

28
00:01:52,388 --> 00:01:56,583
rejects it and creates no successful cache entry. JSON responses are

29
00:01:56,583 --> 00:02:00,778
bounded while reading. The cache also separates otherwise identical requests by

30
00:02:00,778 --> 00:02:04,973
hashed credential identity, so one account cannot reuse another account's inference

31
00:02:04,973 --> 00:02:05,355
result.

32
00:02:05,855 --> 00:02:10,889
The current suite passes all twenty-nine tests. It exercises every split

33
00:02:10,889 --> 00:02:15,924
point for five supported credential formats, normalized private addresses, response bounds,

34
00:02:15,924 --> 00:02:20,958
cancellation, incomplete streams, in-band errors, and account-separated cache behavior. The public

35
00:02:20,958 --> 00:02:25,077
repository includes the deterministic demo and the test commands.

36
00:02:25,577 --> 00:02:29,739
NebiusGuard makes these boundaries inspectable without claiming universal security. URL checks

37
00:02:29,739 --> 00:02:33,900
do not pin DNS or enforce redirects, pattern checks are incomplete

38
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:38,061
by nature, and the audit and cache remain in memory. The

39
00:02:38,061 --> 00:02:42,223
code and captured evidence are public at github dot com slash

40
00:02:42,223 --> 00:02:43,736
sidsri fourteen slash nebiusguard.
